  "record_scope_definition": "Each function record hashes its complete original assembly range; this is an evidence boundary, not a claim that every listed function is fully reconstructed or integrated. The source implementation and external service limits are described in NOTES.md and source_reconstruction_scope.",
  "source_reconstruction_scope": "Bounded Character Limbus/Spawn state kernels, exact-name Script_SpawnCharacter factory request, and directly called source-owned Character services. This is not whole Character/AI/trigger reconstruction.",
  "caller_facts": [
    "Caller resolves an already-loaded Character by exact object name; Script_SpawnCharacter does not allocate one.",
    "The normal character constructor registers state IDs 0 through 19; the port factory also checks the Spawn ID bit before changing state.",
    "Resolved respawn timer eligibility/delay, CanRespawn, group predicates, saved Limbus transform, AI table/type, animation table Spawn sequence, visual property, and body ownership are supplied as explicit adapter facts/services.",
    "The selected development ghosts begin in authored Limbus state 0 and the request asks for Spawn state 1; initial presentation hiding for auto_spawn=0 is separate policy."
  ],
  "unsupported": [
    "GhostAmbushHallway trigger activation and its command table/dispatch timing are not reconstructed.",
    "Autonomous AI, target selection, movement/combat decisions, and AI event production are not reconstructed.",
    "Caller producers for respawn eligibility, group membership/update, saved Limbus transforms, and complete revive/body ownership remain external.",
    "PreSpawn focus and arbitrary transitions into Spawn outside the bounded fresh-ghost path are not reconstructed.",
    "General enable-condition/serialized visibility and full VisualObject synchronization remain external; selected fresh Ghost visibility is now source-bound.",
    "Timed alpha fading is not implemented or claimed; VisualObject::StartFadeIn and UpdateFadeIn are return stubs."
  ],
